# Python Implementation Standards

- Use type hints for public functions and class methods.
- Keep modules cohesive and respect single responsibility.
- Inject external dependencies (browser, DB engine, config) instead of hardcoding them.
- Avoid hidden side effects at import time.
- Raise specific exceptions with clear, user-actionable messages.

# Reliability

- Use retries/backoff only for transient failures.
- Prefer deterministic transformations and explicit validation.
- Keep selector definitions and field mapping centralized and testable.
